<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ibn Jahhaf</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1095">1095</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ibn Jahhaf was the qadi of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a> who in 1092 led a rising that killed al-Qadir, the Castilian client ruler of the city, and appealed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravids</a> for help. Rodrigo Díaz, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-cid">El Cid</a>, besieged Valencia, which surrendered in June 1094. El Cid had Ibn Jahhaf burned to death in 1095.</p></div>
